    (0x5af4e4, 'function', 'DynFpsGovernorTick', 'DynFpsGovernorTick [high] Dynamic-FPS governor: Cap=GetRenFpsCap, clamps Target; DYNAMIC_FPS off -> Target=Cap; Mode 4 steps 120->60->30 (Mode=3); Mode 0 with StepUpCounter < -(fps*1000/60) steps 30->60 or 60->120 (if cap 120); publishes Target to GameMain+0x618 (aka DynFpsTierSelect, DynamicFpsGovernorStep) || also: Dynamic FPS controller (FPS Dynamic Adjustment): picks tier 120/60/30 from CPU-only mon+0x74, writes G[618] at 0x5AF5D2; hosts Nioh3Fix DynFPS setting/target sigs and VRR P8b; cannot see GPU-bound drops | Dynamic-FPS governor (with 0x5af410): steps target 120->60->30 or back when DYNAMIC_FPS (0x45baf58) is on | sig: void DynFpsGovernorTick(DynFpsState* s) | src: re/out/anchors.md §site 0x5af50a; notes/frame-timing.md §0, §3; re/out/README.md §frame pacing; re/settings/live_refs.txt'),
    (0x5af50a, 'label', 'DynFps_SettingCheck', "DynFps_SettingCheck [high] cmp [0x45BAF58],r11d (DYNAMIC_FPS setting read); Nioh3Fix sig #21 'Dynamic FPS setting' (+3 rel). README says Nioh3Fix DynFPS hook sits 0x1C before a VRR site: matches this (P8b=0x5AF526), not the target hook 0x5AF5D2 (aka DynFpsGovernorTick_CheckDynamicFps, DynamicFpsGovernor_CheckDynamicFps) || also: Nioh3Fix site (menu framegen / DYNAMIC_FPS): cmp dword [0x45baf58],r11d (7 B); if DYNAMIC_FPS==0 sets Target=Cap and returns | Nioh3Fix hook site on the DYNAMIC_FPS check inside governor 0x5af4e4 | src: notes/frame-timing.md §3; notes/nioh3fix-signatures.md; mod/Nioh3EngineFix/README.md §Compatibility; re/out/anchors.md §site 0x5af50a; re/out/README.md §frame pacing"),
